title: Security & Defence
subtitle: The Judicial Forces, defence policy and the Senate Guard.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_forces.svg
view-if: security_timer <= 0 and chair_security = "rc" and cardok_security
on-arrival: turn_actions += 1; security_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "security"
new-page: true

= Security & Defence Committee

The Caucus chairs the Security & Defence Committee.

- @judicials: Expand the Judicial Forces.
- @oversight: Bring the army under Senate oversight.
- @guard: Return the Senate Guard to the Senate's command.
- @navy: Shape the Navy's officer appointments.
- @audit: Audit defence procurement.
- @command: Put the Senate Command Act to the Senate.
- @patrols: Deploy regional patrol fleets to the Rim.
- @pirate_campaign: Launch a campaign against the pirate fleets.
- @officers: Open the officer corps to every species.
- @review: Review the Republic's defences.
- @easy_discard

@judicials
view-if: judicial_forces < 8
subtitle: −2 treasury. +1 Judicial Forces, loyal to the Senate.
choose-if: treasury >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 2; judicial_forces += 1; judicial_expansion = 1; sec_relation += 2; hawk_dissent -= 3; mil_invest += 1

New Judicial cruisers are commissioned, crewed by volunteers sworn to the Senate.

@oversight
view-if: not army_oversight and kamino_army and (clones > 0 or kamino_known)
subtitle: −1 political capital. A permanent Senate committee over the army's commanders.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.security_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.4, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.25, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.1, cis: 0.5}, true);
Q.ov_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Grand Army Oversight Act', Q.ov_vote);
if (Q.ov_vote >= 50) { Q.army_oversight = 1; Q.navy_loyalty += 10; this.achieve('oversight'); }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if army_oversight : The Grand Army will answer to a standing Senate committee, which has full access to the army's orders, contingency plans and Kaminoan contracts. ?][? if not army_oversight and not rc_chancellor : The Chancellor's allies argue that "a war cannot be run by committee". The bill fails. ?][? if not army_oversight and rc_chancellor : The Security Bloc argues that "a war cannot be run by committee". The bill fails. ?]

@guard
view-if: not senate_guard_reformed
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Red Guards would answer to the Senate, not the Chancellor.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.45, rim: 0.55, sec: 0.35, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.05, cis: 0.5}, true);
Q.sg_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'oversight');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Senate Guard Restoration Act', Q.sg_vote);
if (Q.sg_vote >= 50) { Q.senate_guard_reformed = 1; Q.pal_relation -= 10; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if senate_guard_reformed : The Senate Guard returns to its ancient blue robes and to the command of the Senate itself. ?][? if not senate_guard_reformed : The Guard remains under the Chancellor's office. ?]

@navy
view-if: clones > 0 and navy_loyalty < 90
subtitle: +8 Navy loyalty to the Senate; the Security Bloc objects.
on-arrival: navy_loyalty += 8; sec_relation -= 4; mil_invest += 1

The committee confirms a slate of officers known for their loyalty to the constitution. A few promising officers whose loyalty runs to [+ pal_title +] rather than to the Senate, such as one Captain Tarkin, are passed over.

@audit
view-if: security_audits < 3
subtitle: −1 corruption; the Security Bloc is annoyed.
on-arrival: corruption -= 1; sec_relation -= 4; treasury += 1; security_audits += 1

The audit finds that the Republic has paid for the same frigate four times.

@review
subtitle: Free. The Hawks appreciate it.
on-arrival: hawk_dissent -= 3; judicial_forces += 0.1

@command
view-if: army_oversight and not senate_command
subtitle: −1 political capital. The army and the Guard take their orders from the Senate, if it agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and senate_guard_reformed
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not senate_guard_reformed : The Senate Guard must answer to the Senate first. ?][? if senate_guard_reformed : Needs 1 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.security_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.4, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.2, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.05, cis: 0.5}, true);
Q.sc_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', '-army']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Senate Command Act', Q.sc_vote);
if (Q.sc_vote >= 50) { Q.senate_command = 1; Q.navy_loyalty += 15; Q.sec_relation -= 6; Q.pal_relation -= 6; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if senate_command : The Senate Command Act passes. Every order to the Grand Army and the Senate Guard must now carry the countersignature of the Senate's defence committee, and every officer swears to the Senate by name. ?][? if not senate_command : The Act fails. The army's chain of command still ends at a single desk. ?]

@patrols
view-if: not patrol_fleets and not hutt_deal
subtitle: −1 political capital. Standing fleets to guard the Rim's trade lanes.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and mil_invest >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if mil_invest < 1 : We need a stronger military first. ?][? if mil_invest >= 1 : Needs 1 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: capital -= 1; patrol_fleets = 1; rim_hardship -= 3; trade += 3; rim_relation += 2; sec_relation += 2; security_timer = 1

Regional patrol fleets take station along the Rimma, the Hydian Way and the Corellian Run. For the first time in a generation, a freighter captain on the Rim can call for help and expect it to come.

@pirate_campaign
view-if: patrol_fleets and not pirates_crushed and not hutt_deal
subtitle: −1 political capital. Take the war to the pirate fleets' havens.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.security_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
if (Q.mil_invest >= 2) { Q.pirates_crushed = 1; Q.fear -= 2; Q.faith += 1; Q.trade += 4; Q.rim_hardship -= 2; Q.sec_relation += 3; SW.momentum(Q, 0.4, 'the rout of the pirate fleets'); }
else { Q.pirate_humiliation = 1; Q.fear += 6; Q.faith -= 3; Q.navy_loyalty -= 5; Q.sec_relation -= 4; SW.momentum(Q, -1, 'a humiliating defeat by the pirates'); }
!}
go-to: pirate_victory if pirates_crushed; pirate_defeat if not pirates_crushed

@pirate_victory

The Republic's task forces strike the pirate havens of the Rim one after another: the asteroid bases of the Cron Drift, the hidden docks of Florrum. The great pirate fleets that have preyed on the trade lanes for a century are broken. Only the syndicates that financed them remain.

@pirate_defeat

The task force is ambushed in the Cron Drift. Three cruisers are lost, two more are captured and paraded on the HoloNet by the pirate lord who took them. The Republic has been humiliated by bandits, and every senator who voted for the campaign is asked why our fleets were not ready.

@officers
view-if: not officer_corps
subtitle: −1 political capital. An officer corps that looks like the Republic.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: capital -= 1; officer_corps = 1; navy_loyalty += 3; hawk_dissent += 2; sec_relation -= 2; security_timer = 1

The committee orders that commissions and promotions be open to every species of the Republic, and reviews every case of an officer passed over for not being human. A good many admirals are quietly furious. A good many captains are not.
